<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE hrc PUBLIC "-//Cail Lomecb//DTD Colorer HRC take5//EN"
  "http://colorer.sf.net/2003/hrc.dtd">
<hrc version="take5" xmlns="http://colorer.sf.net/2003/hrc"
     xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
     xsi:schemaLocation="http://colorer.sf.net/2003/hrc http://colorer.sf.net/2003/hrc.xsd">

<annotation>
   <documentation>
      Dagor shader language (*.dshl), ported to take5 from the 4ever description that ships with Far 2.0
      (Plugins/Colorer/hrc/base/dshl.hrc), so that Far3 and Far 2.0 colour .dshl files identically.

      4ever aliased its regions as below (the &lt;define/&gt; block at the top of the original); the
      take5 parents reproduce the same colours out of the shared palette:
        dNamespace     = dString    -&gt; def:String
        dState         = dString    -&gt; def:String
        dStateValue    = dNumDec    -&gt; def:NumberDec
        dType          = dNumDec    -&gt; def:NumberDec  (4ever *overrode* dType)
        dHlslKeyword   = dParam     -&gt; def:Parameter
        dHlslIntrinsic = dParam     -&gt; def:Parameter
        dHlslType      = dParam     -&gt; def:Parameter
        dHlslSemantic  = dNumDec    -&gt; def:NumberDec
        dHlslPreProc   = dDirective -&gt; def:Directive
        dHlslPreProc2  = dNumHex    -&gt; def:NumberHex
      plus the plain ones: dComment/dError/dString/dSymbol/dKeyword to
      def:Comment/def:Error/def:String/def:Symbol/def:Keyword, dSymbol2 to def:SymbolStrong,
      dpOpenStruct/dpCloseStruct to def:PairStart/def:PairEnd.

      Two spellings differ besides the names: 4ever declares a region alias as
      &lt;define name="dX" value="dY"/&gt; where take5 declares &lt;region name="X" parent="def:Y"/&gt;, and
      4ever writes &lt;virtual subst="s"/&gt; where take5 writes &lt;virtual subst-scheme="s"/&gt;; take5
      ignores the 4ever spelling in silence, which leaves everything inside the substituted scheme unstyled.

      Names had to be spelled exactly here, because take5 resolves them case sensitively while 4ever
      does not: 4ever compares region names with stricmp (shared/colorer/ccdata.cpp,
      CColorData::getregion), so its "dKeyWord" reached the region defined as "dKeyword" and its scheme
      reference "cPrePro"/"cPrePro2" reached "CPrePro"/"CPrePro2".  Neither would resolve in take5, so
      the canonical spellings are used on both sides: def:Keyword here, dKeyword in the 4ever file.

      4ever helper schemes map onto take5 as mCHexNumb/mFloatNumb/mDecNumb to
      def:CHexNumber/def:FloatNumber/def:DecNumber and Comment to def:Comment. mPairedBrackets becomes a
      local PairedBrackets copy below rather than def:PairedBrackets, so the &lt;virtual/&gt; and the
      scheme it substitutes live in the same type.  mStdStr is inlined below so the quotes keep the literal's
      colour, exactly as 4ever painted them.

      Install: copy this file to &lt;Far3&gt;\Plugins\FarColorer\base\auto\ and reload the base
      (F11 -&gt; FarColorer -&gt; Reload base). base\auto\ is a stock folder already registered in
      base\catalog.xml, and this file carries its own &lt;prototype&gt;, so nothing else needs editing.
      Dagor shader (dshl) then stands in the file-type list, which is what shows the prototype registered;
      the schema-library test parses every scheme but iterates registered types only, so it passes without
      proving that this one loaded. A FarColorer update that replaces the whole base folder drops the copy.

      Four take5 traps, none of which reports an error - the rule simply never matches:
        a &lt;prototype&gt; counts only as a direct child of &lt;hrc&gt;. Stock files keep one inside
          &lt;annotation&gt;&lt;appinfo&gt;, but that copy only feeds their build; a type put there loads
          and matches no file.
        a bare '{' or '}' inside a character class is not a literal, so [^\s;${}] has to be written
          [^\s;$\{\}] or the class swallows the brace that ends a block.
        every branch of an alternation is bracketed: (a)|(b)|(c) matches in both engines, while 4ever
          matches nothing at all for a bare a|b|c. This holds for a block start and end as well as for
          &lt;regexp match=.../&gt;, which is why the generated @-binding rules bracket each type name.
          The two inherited preprocessor block ends are the exception on record: they keep their original
          unbracketed form, which renders the same either way.
        word boundaries differ: 4ever reads \b as start-of-word, \B as end-of-word and \c as
          non-word-before, while take5 reads Perl's \b and \B.
   </documentation>
</annotation>

<prototype name="dshl" group="main" description="Dagor shader (dshl)">
   <location link="dshl.hrc"/>
   <filename>/\.dshl$/i</filename>
</prototype>

<type name="dshl">

   <import type="def"/>

   <region name="Comment"       parent="def:Comment"/>
   <region name="Error"         parent="def:Error"/>
   <region name="String"        parent="def:String"/>
   <region name="Symbol"        parent="def:Symbol"/>
   <region name="StructSymbol"  parent="def:SymbolStrong"/>
   <region name="Keyword"       parent="def:Keyword"/>
   <region name="Directive"     parent="def:Directive"/>
   <region name="Namespace"     parent="def:String"/>
   <region name="State"         parent="def:String"/>
   <region name="StateValue"    parent="def:NumberDec"/>
   <region name="Type"          parent="def:NumberDec"/>
   <region name="HlslKeyword"   parent="def:Parameter"/>
   <region name="HlslIntrinsic" parent="def:Parameter"/>
   <region name="HlslType"      parent="def:Parameter"/>
   <region name="HlslSemantic"  parent="def:NumberDec"/>
   <region name="HlslPreProc"   parent="def:Directive"/>
   <region name="HlslPreProc2"  parent="def:NumberHex"/>

   <!-- 4ever mStdStr: quotes share the literal's colour -->
   <!-- 4ever inherited the shared mPairedBrackets and substituted it with the enclosing scheme.  A
        local copy is used here rather than def:PairedBrackets, so the substitution and the scheme it
        substitutes live in the same type, and re-entering the dshl / hlsl scheme inside braces is
        unambiguous. -->
   <scheme name="PairedBrackets">
      <block start="/(\{)/" end="/(\})/" scheme="PairedBrackets"
             region00="StructSymbol" region01="def:PairStart"
             region10="StructSymbol" region11="def:PairEnd"/>
      <block start="/(\()/" end="/(\))/" scheme="PairedBrackets"
             region00="Symbol" region01="def:PairStart"
             region10="Symbol" region11="def:PairEnd"/>
      <block start="/(\[)/" end="/(\])/" scheme="PairedBrackets"
             region00="Symbol" region01="def:PairStart"
             region10="Symbol" region11="def:PairEnd"/>
   </scheme>

   <scheme name="StdString">
      <regexp match='/".*?"/' region0="String"/>
      <regexp match="/'.*?'/" region0="String"/>
   </scheme>

   <scheme name="commonSyntax">
      <inherit scheme="def:CHexNumber"/>
      <inherit scheme="def:FloatNumber"/>
      <inherit scheme="def:DecNumber"/>
      <inherit scheme="StdString"/>
      <regexp match="/\b(0x[\da-fA-F]*?([^\s\W\da-fA-F]).*?)\b/i" region0="Error"/>

      <regexp match="/\/\/.*$/" region0="Comment"/>
      <block  start="/\/\*/" end="/\*\//" scheme="def:Comment"
              region="Comment" region00="def:PairStart" region10="def:PairEnd"/>

      <!-- @-binding types, one rule per PRESHADER_VARIABLE_TYPE_LIST_* group in variantSemantic.h
           plus the state-block binding types. Generated by _colorer_keywords.py. Longest
           alternative first (texCubeArray before texCube before tex), and every branch bracketed:
           4ever matches nothing at all for a bare a|b|c in a match regexp. -->
      <regexp match='/\b[a-zA-Z_]\w*\s*(@)((f43)|(f44)|(f1)|(f2)|(f3)|(f4))\b/' region1="Keyword" region2="String"/> <!-- FLOAT -->
      <regexp match='/\b[a-zA-Z_]\w*\s*(@)((i1)|(i2)|(i3)|(i4))\b/' region1="Keyword" region2="String"/> <!-- INT -->
      <regexp match='/\b[a-zA-Z_]\w*\s*(@)((u1)|(u2)|(u3)|(u4))\b/' region1="Keyword" region2="String"/> <!-- UINT -->
      <regexp match='/\b[a-zA-Z_]\w*\s*(@)((cbuf)|(buf))\b/' region1="Keyword" region2="String"/> <!-- BUF -->
      <regexp match='/\b[a-zA-Z_]\w*\s*(@)((texCubeArray)|(texArray)|(texCube)|(tex2d)|(tex3d)|(tex))\b/' region1="Keyword" region2="String"/> <!-- TEX -->
      <regexp match='/\b[a-zA-Z_]\w*\s*(@)((cmpSampler)|(smpArray)|(sampler)|(smp2d)|(smp3d))\b/' region1="Keyword" region2="String"/> <!-- SMP -->
      <regexp match='/\b[a-zA-Z_]\w*\s*(@)((staticSmpCubeArray)|(staticSmpArray)|(staticSmpCube)|(staticSmp3D)|(staticSmp))\b/' region1="Keyword" region2="String"/> <!-- STATIC_SMP -->
      <regexp match='/\b[a-zA-Z_]\w*\s*(@)((staticTexCubeArray)|(staticTexArray)|(staticTexCube)|(staticTex3D)|(staticTex))\b/' region1="Keyword" region2="String"/> <!-- STATIC_TEX -->
      <regexp match='/\b[a-zA-Z_]\w*\s*(@)((tlas)|(uav))\b/' region1="Keyword" region2="String"/> <!-- OTHER -->
      <regexp match='/\b[a-zA-Z_]\w*\s*(@)((bindlessTexCubeArray)|(bindlessByteBuffer)|(bindlessTexArray)|(bindlessSampler)|(bindlessTexCube)|(bindlessTex2D)|(bindlessTex3D))\b/' region1="Keyword" region2="String"/> <!-- BINDLESS -->
      <regexp match='/\b[a-zA-Z_]\w*\s*(@)((subpass_read))\b/' region1="Keyword" region2="String"/> <!-- SUBPASS_READ -->
      <regexp match='/\b[a-zA-Z_]\w*\s*(@)((ps_output))\b/' region1="Keyword" region2="String"/> <!-- STATE_BLOCK -->

      <keywords region="HlslPreProc2">
         <word name="globtm"/>
         <word name="immediate_dword_count"/>
         <word name="local_view_pos"/>
         <word name="local_view_x"/>
         <word name="local_view_y"/>
         <word name="local_view_z"/>
         <word name="projtm"/>
         <word name="viewprojtm"/>
         <word name="world_local_pos"/>
         <word name="world_local_x"/>
         <word name="world_local_y"/>
         <word name="world_local_z"/>
      </keywords>

      <keywords region="Symbol">
         <symb name=";"/>
         <symb name="="/>
         <symb name="+"/>
         <symb name="-"/>
         <symb name="/"/>
         <symb name="*"/>
         <symb name="&amp;"/>
         <symb name="|"/>
         <symb name="^"/>
         <symb name="("/>
         <symb name=")"/>
         <symb name="["/>
         <symb name="]"/>
         <symb name=","/>
         <symb name="."/>
         <symb name=":"/>
         <symb name="!"/>
         <symb name="~"/>
         <symb name="&lt;"/>
         <symb name="&gt;"/>
         <symb name="%"/>
         <symb name="?"/>
         <symb name="#"/>
      </keywords>
   </scheme>

   <!-- the stage block gets a scheme of its own so the braces of a '@f44 = { ... }' binding value
        open a nested block; without one the block's own end takes the '}' of that value and closes
        early. It cannot live in commonSyntax: hlsl reaches that through hlslBase, and a brace inside
        an hlsl body would switch to it and lose every HLSL keyword. -->
   <scheme name="stageBlock">
      <inherit scheme="commonSyntax"/>
      <inherit scheme="PairedBrackets">
         <virtual scheme="PairedBrackets" subst-scheme="stageBlock"/>
      </inherit>
   </scheme>

   <scheme name="CPrePro">
      <inherit scheme="commonSyntax"/>

      <keywords region="HlslPreProc">
         <word name="declare"/>
         <word name="elif"/>
         <word name="else"/>
         <word name="endif"/>
         <word name="error"/>
         <word name="if"/>
      </keywords>
   </scheme>

   <scheme name="CPrePro2">
      <inherit scheme="commonSyntax"/>

      <keywords region="HlslPreProc2">
         <word name="pragma"/>
         <word name="define"/>
         <word name="undef"/>
         <word name="elif"/>
         <word name="else"/>
         <word name="endif"/>
         <word name="error"/>
         <word name="if"/>
         <word name="ifdef"/>
         <word name="ifndef"/>
         <word name="include"/>
         <word name="line"/>
         <word name="__LINE__"/>
         <word name="__FILE__"/>
      </keywords>
   </scheme>

   <scheme name="hlslBase">
      <block  start="/^\s*##/" end="/^ | ([^\\]?#1) $/x" scheme="CPrePro"  region="HlslPreProc"/>
      <block  start="/^\s*#/"  end="/^ | ([^\\]?#1) $/x" scheme="CPrePro2" region="HlslPreProc2"/>
      <inherit scheme="commonSyntax"/>

      <regexp match="/\b((bool)|(int)|(uint)|(fixed)|(half)|(float)|(double))[1-4]\b/" region0="HlslType"/>
      <regexp match="/\b((bool)|(int)|(uint)|(fixed)|(half)|(float)|(double))[1-4]x[1-4]\b/" region0="HlslType"/>

      <keywords region="HlslKeyword" ignorecase="yes">
         <word name="BlendState"/>
         <word name="Bool"/>
         <word name="Break"/>
         <word name="Case"/>
         <word name="CBuffer"/>
         <word name="Class"/>
         <word name="Compile"/>
         <word name="Const"/>
         <word name="Continue"/>
         <word name="Default"/>
         <word name="DepthStencilState"/>
         <word name="DepthStencilView"/>
         <word name="Discard"/>
         <word name="Do"/>
         <word name="Double"/>
         <word name="Else"/>
         <word name="Enum"/>
         <word name="Extern"/>
         <word name="False"/>
         <word name="Float"/>
         <word name="For"/>
         <word name="GeometryShader"/>
         <word name="Half"/>
         <word name="If"/>
         <word name="In"/>
         <word name="Inline"/>
         <word name="Inout"/>
         <word name="Int"/>
         <word name="Matrix"/>
         <word name="Namespace"/>
         <word name="Nointerpolation"/>
         <word name="Operator"/>
         <word name="Out"/>
         <word name="Pass"/>
         <word name="PixelShader"/>
         <word name="RasterizerState"/>
         <word name="RenderTargetView"/>
         <word name="Return"/>
         <word name="Register"/>
         <word name="Sampler"/>
         <word name="sampler"/>
         <word name="Sampler1D"/>
         <word name="Sampler2D"/>
         <word name="Sampler3D"/>
         <word name="SamplerCUBE"/>
         <word name="hsampler"/>
         <word name="hsampler1D"/>
         <word name="hsampler2D"/>
         <word name="hsampler3D"/>
         <word name="hsamplerCUBE"/>
         <word name="fxsampler"/>
         <word name="fxsampler1D"/>
         <word name="fxsampler2D"/>
         <word name="fxsampler3D"/>
         <word name="fxsamplerCUBE"/>
         <word name="fltsampler"/>
         <word name="fltsampler1D"/>
         <word name="fltsampler2D"/>
         <word name="fltsampler3D"/>
         <word name="fltsamplerCUBE"/>
         <word name="sampler_state"/>
         <word name="SamplerComparisonState"/>
         <word name="Shared"/>
         <word name="Sizeof"/>
         <word name="Stateblock"/>
         <word name="Stateblock_state"/>
         <word name="Static"/>
         <word name="String"/>
         <word name="Struct"/>
         <word name="Switch"/>
         <word name="TBuffer"/>
         <word name="Technique"/>
         <word name="Technique10"/>
         <word name="Template"/>
         <word name="texture1"/>
         <word name="Texture1D"/>
         <word name="Texture1D"/>
         <word name="Texture1DArray"/>
         <word name="texture2D"/>
         <word name="Texture2D"/>
         <word name="Texture2DArray"/>
         <word name="Texture2DMS"/>
         <word name="Texture2DMSArray"/>
         <word name="texture3D"/>
         <word name="Texture3D"/>
         <word name="texturecube"/>
         <word name="TextureCube"/>
         <word name="This"/>
         <word name="True"/>
         <word name="Typedef"/>
         <word name="Typename"/>
         <word name="Uniform"/>
         <word name="Unsigned"/>
         <word name="Using"/>
         <word name="Vector"/>
         <word name="VertexShader"/>
         <word name="Void"/>
         <word name="Volatile"/>
         <word name="While"/>
      </keywords>

      <keywords region="HlslIntrinsic">
         <word name="abs"/>
         <word name="acos"/>
         <word name="all"/>
         <word name="any"/>
         <word name="asfloat"/>
         <word name="asin"/>
         <word name="asint"/>
         <word name="asuint"/>
         <word name="atan"/>
         <word name="atan2"/>
         <word name="ceil"/>
         <word name="clamp"/>
         <word name="clip"/>
         <word name="cos"/>
         <word name="cosh"/>
         <word name="cross"/>
         <word name="D3DCOLORtoUBYTE4"/>
         <word name="ddx"/>
         <word name="ddy"/>
         <word name="degrees"/>
         <word name="determinant"/>
         <word name="distance"/>
         <word name="dot"/>
         <word name="exp"/>
         <word name="exp2"/>
         <word name="faceforward"/>
         <word name="floor"/>
         <word name="fmod"/>
         <word name="frac"/>
         <word name="frexp"/>
         <word name="fwidth"/>
         <word name="GetRenderTargetSampleCount"/>
         <word name="GetRenderTargetSamplePosition"/>
         <word name="isfinite"/>
         <word name="isinf"/>
         <word name="isnan"/>
         <word name="ldexp"/>
         <word name="length"/>
         <word name="lerp"/>
         <word name="lit"/>
         <word name="log"/>
         <word name="log10"/>
         <word name="log2"/>
         <word name="max"/>
         <word name="min"/>
         <word name="modf"/>
         <word name="mul"/>
         <word name="noise"/>
         <word name="normalize"/>
         <word name="pow"/>
         <word name="radians"/>
         <word name="reflect"/>
         <word name="refract"/>
         <word name="round"/>
         <word name="rsqrt"/>
         <word name="saturate"/>
         <word name="sign"/>
         <word name="sin"/>
         <word name="sincos"/>
         <word name="sinh"/>
         <word name="smoothstep"/>
         <word name="sqrt"/>
         <word name="step"/>
         <word name="tan"/>
         <word name="tanh"/>
         <word name="tex1D"/>
         <word name="tex1Dbias"/>
         <word name="tex1Dgrad"/>
         <word name="tex1Dlod"/>
         <word name="tex1Dproj"/>
         <word name="tex2D"/>
         <word name="tex2Dbias"/>
         <word name="tex2Dgrad"/>
         <word name="tex2Dlod"/>
         <word name="tex2Dproj"/>
         <word name="tex3D"/>
         <word name="tex3Dbias"/>
         <word name="tex3Dgrad"/>
         <word name="tex3Dlod"/>
         <word name="tex3Dproj"/>
         <word name="texCUBE"/>
         <word name="texCUBEbias"/>
         <word name="texCUBEgrad"/>
         <word name="texCUBElod"/>
         <word name="texCUBEproj"/>
         <word name="h4tex2D"/>
         <word name="h4tex2Dbias"/>
         <word name="h4tex2Dgrad"/>
         <word name="h4tex2Dlod"/>
         <word name="h4tex2Dproj"/>
         <word name="h4tex3D"/>
         <word name="h4tex3Dbias"/>
         <word name="h4tex3Dgrad"/>
         <word name="h4tex3Dlod"/>
         <word name="h4tex3Dproj"/>
         <word name="h4texCUBE"/>
         <word name="h4texCUBEbias"/>
         <word name="h4texCUBEgrad"/>
         <word name="h4texCUBElod"/>
         <word name="h4texCUBEproj"/>
         <word name="transpose"/>
      </keywords>

      <!-- Reserved keywords -->
      <keywords region="Error">
         <word name="catch"/>
         <word name="char"/>
         <word name="const_cast"/>
         <word name="delete"/>
         <word name="dynamic_cast"/>
         <word name="explicit"/>
         <word name="friend"/>
         <word name="goto"/>
         <word name="long"/>
         <word name="mutable"/>
         <word name="new"/>
         <word name="private"/>
         <word name="protected"/>
         <word name="public"/>
         <word name="reinterpret_cast"/>
         <word name="short"/>
         <word name="signed"/>
         <word name="static_cast"/>
         <word name="throw"/>
         <word name="try"/>
         <word name="union"/>
         <word name="virtual"/>
      </keywords>

      <regexp match="/\b((SV_IsFrontFace)|(SV_InstanceID)|(SV_Depth)|(SV_Position)|(SV_Target)|(COLOR)|(NORMAL)|(POSITION))[0-1]\b/" region0="HlslSemantic"/>
      <regexp match="/\bTEXCOORD[0-9]\b/" region0="HlslSemantic"/>
      <regexp match="/\bTEXCOORD1[0-5]\b/" region0="HlslSemantic"/>

      <keywords region="HlslSemantic">
         <word name="BINORMAL"/>
         <word name="BINORMAL0"/>
         <word name="BLENDINDICES"/>
         <word name="BLENDINDICES0"/>
         <word name="BLENDWEIGHT"/>
         <word name="BLENDWEIGHT0"/>
         <word name="COLOR"/>
         <word name="NORMAL"/>
         <word name="POSITION"/>
         <word name="POSITIONT"/>
         <word name="PSIZE"/>
         <word name="TANGENT"/>
         <word name="TANGENT0"/>
         <word name="TEXCOORD"/>
         <word name="FOG"/>
         <word name="PSIZE"/>
         <word name="PSIZE0"/>
         <word name="TESSFACTOR"/>
         <word name="TESSFACTOR0"/>
         <word name="VFACE"/>
         <word name="VPOS"/>
         <word name="DEPTH"/>
         <word name="DEPTH0"/>
      </keywords>
   </scheme>

   <scheme name="hlslBlock">
      <inherit scheme="hlslBase"/>
      <!-- The braces take their pair regions from a regexp rather than a block: a block would consume
           the '}' aligned with the 'hlsl' keyword, which the enclosing block has to close on. A regexp
           only marks, so that block still sees its end, and the marks are matched by nesting. -->
      <regexp match="/(\{)/" region0="StructSymbol" region1="def:PairStart"/>
      <regexp match="/(\})/" region0="StructSymbol" region1="def:PairEnd"/>
   </scheme>

   <scheme name="hlsl">
      <inherit scheme="hlslBase"/>
      <inherit scheme="PairedBrackets">
         <virtual scheme="PairedBrackets" subst-scheme="hlsl"/>
      </inherit>
   </scheme>

   <scheme name="dshl">
      <inherit scheme="PairedBrackets">
         <virtual scheme="PairedBrackets" subst-scheme="dshl"/>
      </inherit>

      <block start="/^\s*(hlsl)\s*(\(\s*(([acdeghlmpv]s)|([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]{2,}))\s*\))?\s*(\{)\s*/" end="/\s*(\})/"
             scheme="hlsl"
             region00="StructSymbol" region06="def:PairStart"
             region10="StructSymbol" region11="def:PairEnd"/>
      <block start="/^\s*\(\s*(([cpvm]s)|([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]{2,}))\s*\)\s*(\{)\s*/" end="/\s*(\})/"
             scheme="stageBlock"
             region00="StructSymbol" region04="def:PairStart"
             region10="StructSymbol" region11="def:PairEnd"/>

      <!-- hlsl / hlsl(vs) with the opening brace on the following line. \y1 links the end regexp
           back to bracket 1 of start (the indentation), so the block closes on the '}' aligned
           with 'hlsl'. Its def:PairEnd is answered by the def:PairStart that hlslBlock puts on the
           first brace, the one a line below the header, so the pair spans the whole body. -->
      <block start="/^(\s*)(hlsl)\s*(\(\s*(([acdeghlmpv]s)|([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]{2,}))\s*\))?\s*$/" end="/^\y1(\})/"
             scheme="hlslBlock"
             region02="Keyword"
             region10="StructSymbol" region11="def:PairEnd"/>
      <regexp match="/^\s*(hlsl)\s*(\(\s*((([acdeghlmpv]s)|([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]{2,}))\s*\))?![^)]*\))\s*\{?\s*$/" region2="Error"/>
      <regexp match="/^\s*(\(\s*((([cpvm]s)|([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]{2,}))\s*\))?![^)]*\))\s*\{?\s*$/" region1="Error"/>

      <inherit scheme="commonSyntax"/>

      <keywords region="Keyword">
         <word name="allow_opacity_micromaps"/>
         <word name="always_referenced"/>
         <word name="assume"/>
         <word name="assume_if_not_assumed"/>
         <word name="block"/>
         <word name="bounding_pack"/>
         <word name="buffer"/>
         <word name="channel"/>
         <word name="compile"/>
         <word name="const"/>
         <word name="const_buffer"/>
         <word name="dont_render"/>
         <word name="dynamic"/>
         <word name="else"/>
         <word name="error"/>
         <word name="framebuffer_layout"/>
         <word name="global"/>
         <word name="hardware"/>
         <word name="if"/>
         <word name="immediate_dword_count"/>
         <word name="interval"/>
         <word name="literal"/>
